      "note": "modals.tsx ConfirmPrompt (Yes/No/Cancel) is the text editor's dirty-buffer guard. Reached here through its consumer: open the Text editor, dirty the buffer ([data-txted-area]), then click Open ([data-txted-open]) — guard() sees dirty and shows the [data-confirmprompt] modal. Trigger clicks Cancel ([data-answer=cancel]); the prompt closes and the editor stays open with no save/open side effect. Yes/No are deliberately not driven because their 'proceed' path opens the browser file picker, which cannot be driven headlessly."
